1qed|n|A recitation or song of a rhapsodist; a portion of an epic poem adapted for recitation, or usually recited, at one time; hence, a division of the Iliad or the Odyssey; -- called also a book. ; A disconnected series of sentences or statements composed under excitement, and without dependence or natural connection; rambling composition. ; A composition irregular in form, like an improvisation; as, Liszt's "Hungarian Rhapsodies."	a:8f4,172,5;kvd,119,4~8f4,172,5;kvd,119,4	n:8f4,149,1~8f4,149,1
